@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@sku = 7891234567890
@fileName = 7891234567890.foreground.png
@productImagesKey = {{$processEnv CAGE_PRODUCT_IMAGES_TEST_KEY}}

### Get the full shared snapshot, including permanent tombstones
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}

### Upload a raw PNG (point this file reference at an existing local image)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/{{fileName}}
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}
Content-Type: image/png

< ./7891234567890.foreground.png

### Different bytes at the same identity return 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/{{fileName}}
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}
Content-Type: image/png

< ./different-image.foreground.png

### Download an active image (raw image bytes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/{{fileName}}
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}

### Legacy JPG images use the same endpoint and retain their original file name
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/legacy-photo.jpg
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./legacy-photo.jpg

### Global, idempotent deletion creates a permanent tombstone (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/{{fileName}}
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}

### A deleted reference returns 410 and cannot be restored by PUT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references/{{sku}}/{{fileName}}
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}

### The tombstone remains in every full snapshot
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cageouts/product-image-references
X-Product-Images-Key: {{productImagesKey}}
